<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaero of Baekje</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 455–475</span> · Also known as King Gaero</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaero was the twenty-first king of Baekje, reigning from 455 to 475. He sought help from the Chinese Northern Wei against Goguryeo, without success, and carried out costly building works. In 475 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jangsu-of-goguryeo">King Jangsu</a> of Goguryeo took the Baekje capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Hanseong</a> and executed him, forcing Baekje to move its capital south to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gongju">Ungjin</a>.</p></div>
